 "path": "arc-divider-recolor/SKILL.md",
 "edits": [
  {
   "oldText": "description: Solve ARC grids split by a solid divider, where demonstrations identify which panel supplies the output and how its cells are mapped.",
   "newText": "description: Solve ARC grids split by a solid divider by inferring panel selection, alignment, or cross-panel cell mappings from demonstrations."
  },
  {
   "oldText": "1. In every demonstration, locate the solid divider and measure the panels. Compare output dimensions and cell patterns against each panel (including rotations/reflections only when evidence supports them); determine whether output copies one panel, transforms it, or compares corresponding cells. Do not assume the lower or first panel is selected from orientation alone.\n2. Derive the mapping and any cross-panel rule cell by cell from demonstrations. Test every output cell, including cases where candidate inputs differ; reject any rule that misses even one location. Distinguish the candidate's exact condition (for example, a particular color pairing) from merely being in a panel, and track row/column offsets, crop, orientation, and panel dimensions explicitly. If more than one rule fits or none fits, request another demo rather than guessing.\n3. Apply only the fully verified rule to the test. Construct the exact demonstrated output dimensions and cell values; independently check each qualifying and nonqualifying position and the separator exclusion before submitting.",
   "newText": "1. Locate the solid divider in each demo and measure the panels. Compare output dimensions and patterns with each panel; consider rotations, reflections, cropping, or offsets only when supported by evidence. Do not select the first or lower panel from orientation alone.\n2. Determine whether the output copies/transforms a panel or combines corresponding cells. Infer exact positional and color conditions, including which candidate input qualifies; distinguish these from merely belonging to a panel. If the rule is ambiguous or no candidate fits, follow the demo-request procedure in `arc-stream-actions` rather than guessing.\n3. Apply the demonstrated mapping, preserving its panel dimensions, alignment, and exclusion of the separator. Follow `arc-stream-actions` for cross-demo validation, output checks, and the action protocol."
  }
 ]
}

